1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:04,175
Your new retriever can be better, and
still look worse in your eval.

2
00:00:05,183 --> 00:00:10,389
If your relevance labels come only from the
current system's results, documents it

3
00:00:10,389 --> 00:00:12,483
never returned were never judged.

4
00:00:13,083 --> 00:00:18,018
So when the new retriever finds them, they
count as non-relevant, and a better

5
00:00:18,018 --> 00:00:19,283
system scores worse.

6
00:00:20,283 --> 00:00:22,483
The fix is pooled judgments.

7
00:00:22,783 --> 00:00:27,233
Label the union of the top 20 from
every system under test.

8
00:00:27,533 --> 00:00:31,208
Then the eval isn't biased toward the
system you already run.

9
00:00:32,217 --> 00:00:34,842
The full article is on vidyal.ai.
